<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR rates largely higher.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR rates largely higher.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) were largely higher on Monday in the wake of a possible rise in U.S. interest rates, traders said.</p>
<p>Likewise, domestic interest rates are now seen to have reached their bottom and correct upwards, they said.</p>
<p>Only the three-month and six-month rates were unchanged.</p>
<p>PHIBOR represents rates at which banks are willing to swap pesos for dollars.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			 MARCH 24		 MARCH 21</p>
<p>    1 W		8  3/4		  8  5/8</p>
<p>    2 W		8 11/16		 8  9/16</p>
<p>    1 M		8  3/4		  8 11/16</p>
<p>    2 M		8 13/16		 8  3/4</p>
<p>    3 M		8 13/16		 8 13/16</p>
<p>    6 M		9  1/8		  9  1/16</p>
<p>    12M		9  9/16		 9  1/2</p>
<p>    VAL		25-Mar		  24-Mar</p>
<p>--LILIAN KARUNUNGAN (632) 841-8937</p>
</text>
